-------------------------------------------------------------------

ML505 demo board PDL examples:

We currently provide two different binaries, ML505 and ML505SPI, each handling a PDL for one different protocol (respectively JTAG and SPI).

Each binary may be launched for example, with the following command: ./ML505 <path_to_ml505_jtag_sit_file> .

------- Using the JTAG interface with the ML505 demo board:

The ML505 provides a JTAG interface with a 11-bit instruction register, and two 16-bit data register. These latter have respectively the following IR address: 0x01 and 0x02.

Data register 0x01 contains the amplitude on a 0->255 dynamic of each channel (8-bit MSb are left channel, while 8-bit LSb are right channel) that the VU-meter must display.

Data register 0x02 contains the ADC latest sampled value. Data is set on 16-bit in the same way than in data register 0x01.

To execute the dedicated PDLs with the ML505 JTAG slave, please use the following command: ./ML505 <path_to_ml505_jtag_sit_file>/SIT/ml505_demo.sit

------- Using the SPI interface with the ML505 demo board:

The ML505 MAST prototype contains a SPI-slave with an 8-bit data register, connected to the front LEDs of the board.

Each SPI packet is at least 2-bytes long, with the first byte containing a read/write command.

SPI master can read the content of the data register with the 0x90 command. Writing requires the master to send the 0x80 command.

To execute the dedicated PDLs with the SPI protocol, please enter the following command:
./ML505 <path_to_ml505_jtag_sit_file>/SIT/ml505_spi.sit
